  "title": "Global spread of Christianity after 1500",
  "summary": "European colonization of the Americas was presented by its victors as bringing civilization and converting Indigenous people to Christianity, a story now challenged for its cultural losses and human rights abuses. In Goa, the Portuguese-era churches, including the tomb of St Francis Xavier, illustrate the evangelization of Asia, and from the 16th to 18th centuries spread European art across the region.",
